### 2026-10-09: Tried Running a URL in Bash

#### Symptoms

Entered:

```bash
http://100.81.140.115:8080/videos/test.mp4
```

into the terminal.

Received:

```bash
-bash: No such file or directory
```

#### Cause

A web URL is not a Linux command.

#### Fix

Open the URL in a browser instead.

Example:

```text
http://100.81.140.115:8080/videos/test.mp4
```

#### Lesson Learned

If it begins with:

```text
http://
```

it belongs in a browser, not a shell.

